        "# Independent Investigation: Coffee House Coupon Acceptance\n",
        "\n",
        "Following the methodology used for bar coupons, this independent investigation focuses on **Coffee House** coupons—the largest single coupon category in the dataset (**3,996 offers** out of 12,684 total).\n",
        "\n",
        "The baseline acceptance rate for Coffee House coupons across all scenarios is **49.92%** (1,995 accepted vs. 2,001 rejected). Below is an exploratory breakdown identifying key driver characteristics, situational contexts, and high-converting segments.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## 1. Primary Factors Influencing Coffee House Coupon Acceptance\n",
        "\n",
        "### A. Prior Habit & Visit Frequency\n",
        "* **Never Go (`never`):** **18.88%** acceptance ($175 / 927$)\n",
        "* **Infrequent Goers (`less1`):** **48.04%** acceptance ($551 / 1,147$)\n",
        "* **Frequent Goers (`1~3`, `4~8`, `gt8`):** **66.02%** acceptance ($1,269 / 1,922$)\n",
        "* **Takeaway:** Drivers who already visit coffee houses more than once a month accept coupons at **more than $3.5\\times$ the rate** of non-goers ($66.02\\%$ vs. $18.88\\%$).\n",
        "\n",
        "### B. Time of Day\n",
        "* **10 AM (Morning Peak):** **64.07%** acceptance ($576 / 899$)\n",
        "* **2 PM (Afternoon Slump):** **54.79%** acceptance ($435 / 794$)\n",
        "* **7 AM (Commute):** **44.58%** acceptance ($407 / 913$)\n",
        "* **6 PM & 10 PM (Evening/Night):** **41.26%** and **42.42%** respectively\n",
        "* **Takeaway:** Mid-morning (**10 AM**) is the prime conversion window, whereas early morning commuters (7 AM) are often on tight schedules and decline coupons more frequently.\n",
        "\n",
        "### C. Passenger Profile & Social Context\n",
        "* **Friend(s):** **59.69%** acceptance ($733 / 1,228$)\n",
        "* **Partner:** **57.05%** acceptance ($174 / 305$)\n",
        "* **Kid(s):** **48.31%** acceptance ($100 / 207$)\n",
        "* **Alone:** **43.79%** acceptance ($988 / 2,256$)\n",
        "* **Takeaway:** Traveling with social companions (**friends or a partner**) increases coffee coupon acceptance by **~14–16 percentage points** over driving alone.\n",
        "\n",
        "### D. Expiration Duration\n",
        "* **1 Day Expiration (`1d`):** **58.39%** acceptance ($1,033 / 1,769$)\n",
        "* **2 Hours Expiration (`2h`):** **43.20%** acceptance ($962 / 2,227$)\n",
        "* **Takeaway:** Longer validity gives drivers time flexibility, boosting acceptance by **+15.19 percentage points**.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## 2. Multi-Variable Subgroup Comparisons\n",
        "\n",
        "| Subgroup Segment | Criteria | Count | Accepted | Acceptance Rate |\n",
        "| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n",
        "| **Frequent Coffee Goers** | Coffee House visits $>1$/month | 1,922 | 1,269 | **66.02%** |\n",
        "| **Segment A (Time Focus)** | Frequent Goer **AND** Time is 10 AM or 2 PM | 811 | 628 | **77.44%** |\n",
        "| **Segment B (Social Focus)** | Frequent Goer **AND** Traveling with Friends or Partner | 724 | 555 | **76.66%** |\n",
        "| **Segment C (Destination)** | Frequent Goer **AND** Destination = 'No Urgent Place' | 1,039 | 768 | **73.92%** |\n",
        "| **Non-Target Segment** | Infrequent/Non-Goers ($\\le 1$/mo) | 2,074 | 726 | **35.00%** |\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## 3. Hypotheses & Characteristics of Drivers Who Accept Coffee Coupons\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Social Coffee Culture Over Solo Convenience:**  \n",
        "   Drivers traveling with friends or partners treat a coffee offer as a casual, shared activity, leading to higher conversion than solo drivers who may be focused strictly on reaching a destination.\n",
        "2. **Time Flexibility & Urgency Drive Action:**  \n",
        "   The mid-morning hours (**10 AM**) combined with an unhurried destination (\"No Urgent Place\") provide the ideal psychological opening for a coffee break. Conversely, rushing to work at 7 AM creates time resistance.\n",
        "3. **Behavioral Habit Trumps Promotion Value:**  \n",
        "   Coupons do not create new coffee drinkers; they merely incentivize existing coffee consumers. Sending coffee coupons to non-visitors yields an abysmal **18.88%** acceptance rate."
